---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure | The Good Present"
  description="A plain-language explanation of affiliate links and editorial independence at The Good Present."
>
  <article class="prose-page shell">
    <header class="prose-page__hero prose-page__hero--compact">
      <p class="eyebrow">Affiliate disclosure</p>
      <h1>Commercial links, clearly explained.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The Good Present may earn a commission when you follow a qualifying merchant link and make a
        purchase.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-page__grid">
      <aside class="disclosure-stamp">
        <span aria-hidden="true">$</span>
        <strong>Affiliate-funded</strong>
        <p>Editorially selected</p>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What that means</h2>
        <p>
          Some product links are affiliate links. If a purchase qualifies, the merchant may pay The
          Good Present a commission. The merchant—not this website—controls the product page,
          transaction, current price, shipping, returns, and other purchase terms.
        </p>

        <h2>What it does not mean</h2>
        <p>
          An affiliate relationship does not allow a merchant to add a product to a guide or supply
          our recommendation copy. We do not show fake ratings, fake discounts, stock claims, or
          countdowns to pressure a decision.
        </p>

        <h2>Development catalog notice</h2>
        <p>
          The current demonstration catalog uses visibly labeled links to <code>example.com</code>.
          They show where a merchant link will appear; they are not production shopping destinations
          and must be replaced with verified editorial data before launch.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choice stays yours</h2>
        <p>
          You never need to use a link from The Good Present. Compare options, check the merchant's
          current information, and choose what fits the recipient and your budget.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
